      ":question/problem": "The volume of space $V$ a particular gas occupies, measured in liters $(L)$, is directly proportional to its temperature $T$, measured in Kelvin $(K)$. The volume of the gas is $V = 48L$ when its temperature is $T = 360K$. Find the volume of the gas when its temperature is $300K$.The volume of the gas is\n{{field-1}} $L$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
